RenHDrum 0.6.0, the upstream release binary
https://github.com/trzz1214/RenHDrum/tree/v0.6.0
https://github.com/trzz1214/RenHDrum/releases/tag/v0.6.0

Since 0.4.0 the upstream build links the C runtime statically (.cargo/config.toml sets
-C target-feature=+crt-static for x86_64-pc-windows-msvc), so the release binary is
shipped here as it is: no rebuild is needed for players without the Visual C++
redistributable. renhdrum.dll is the release asset byte for byte (915456 bytes), and its
sha256 matches the one on the release page. Its dependencies:

    api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0.dll
    KERNEL32.dll
    ntdll.dll

No VCRUNTIME140.dll, no MSVCP140.dll, no api-ms-win-crt-*.dll. It exports 90 names, the
50 of 0.4.0 among them; renhdrum_version() returns 0x000600.

renhdrum.h is include/renhdrum.h from the v0.6.0 tag, byte for byte. The release asset
of the same name differs only in its CRLF line endings
(sha256 664575d5a67fc52ede8a5405ecce4a925a1e96c2f985a35774e4d6ade860a621).

1e266ce970876c025dadba5780fde00f081c5f6dd474b9946af3cea7cbca6026  renhdrum.dll
4ae84d0c60549525d9af95ae24e97f7a4d8f795098c753654793fc607d13e4a4  renhdrum.h

LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE and NOTICE are copied from the same tag: the core of
RenHDrum is dual licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0, and NOTICE asks for
"Copyright (c) 2026 Three-Dola" to be kept. Since 0.5.0 the binary has libopus 1.5.2
statically linked (BSD-3-Clause, for the DualSense speaker over Bluetooth): LICENSE-opus is vendor/opus/COPYING from the same tag, with
LF line endings. The GPL-3.0-or-later parts of that project (integrations/brontide,
integrations/recomp-c/reference) are not used here: the host calls the prebuilt library
through its C ABI and does not build any of its sources.
